            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for smelly, then the Persian for a water heater."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: درخواست کردن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "درخواست کردن (darkhâst kardan) — \"to request, to ask for (formally)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "از مدیر هتل یک اتاق دیگر درخواست کردیم. Az modir-e hotel yek otâq-e digar darkhâst kardim. We asked the hotel manager for another room."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "darkhâst 'a request' + kardan. The person asked takes az."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "darkhâst kardan is built from darkhâst 'a request', which EtymDB lists and which is built on khâstan 'to want', and kardan 'to do', inherited from Middle Persian kardan (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
