          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "irâd gereftan is built from irâd 'an objection, a flaw', a loan usually traced to Arabic īrād 'bringing forward', and the native verb gereftan 'to take'. EtymDB does not list irâd."
